# Implementation Plan — Decoupled Payment Provider Strategy Pattern

This plan outlines abstracting payment gateway implementations behind a unified **Payment Provider Interface** (Strategy Pattern). This structure decouples the core billing system from any specific payment gateway (such as Paystack) and allows switching or adding providers (e.g. Paystack, Stripe, Flutterwave) dynamically via configuration.

## Proposed Changes

### Payment Provider Abstraction Layer

#### [NEW] [types.ts](file:///c:/Users/ohioa/Projects/React/logged/lib/billing/providers/types.ts)
Define the unified `PaymentProvider` contract:
```ts
export interface PaymentProvider {
  name: string;
  createCustomer(params: { email: string; name?: string }): Promise<{ customerCode: string }>;
  initializeCheckout(params: {
    email: string;
    amount: number;
    planCode?: string;
    callbackUrl?: string;
    metadata?: Record<string, unknown>;
  }): Promise<{ authorizationUrl: string; reference: string }>;
  chargeAuthorization(params: {
    authorizationCode: string;
    email: string;
    amount: number;
    metadata?: Record<string, unknown>;
  }): Promise<{ reference: string }>;
  cancelSubscription(subscriptionCode: string, token?: string): Promise<boolean>;
  verifyWebhookSignature(rawBody: string, signature: string | null): boolean;
  parseWebhookEvent(rawBody: string): {
    eventType: string;
    providerEventId: string;
    userId?: string;
    customerCode?: string;
    subscriptionCode?: string;
    planCode?: string;
    metadata?: Record<string, unknown>;
    raw: unknown;
  };
}
```

#### [NEW] [paystack.ts](file:///c:/Users/ohioa/Projects/React/logged/lib/billing/providers/paystack.ts)
Implement `PaystackPaymentProvider` adhering to `PaymentProvider`, wrapping underlying `lib/paystack/` calls.

#### [NEW] [index.ts](file:///c:/Users/ohioa/Projects/React/logged/lib/billing/providers/index.ts)
- Maintain provider registry (`paystack` by default, expandable to `stripe`, `flutterwave`, etc.).
- Export `getPaymentProvider(name?: string)` which resolves provider based on DB setting `payment_provider` or env var `PAYMENT_PROVIDER` (defaulting to `"paystack"`).

